{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24345 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Parameritannin A-1 is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step pathway involving leukocyte antigen CD37. This pathway begins with Parameritannin A-1 acting as a target on CD37, which in turn is targeted by a metabolite of demethylated glycyrol. This metabolite, in turn, directly targets DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that Parameritannin A-1 exerts its effect on CD37, which then modulates the activity of DNA polymerase iota through a chain of molecular interactions. The presence of multiple distinct metabolites targeting DNA polymerase iota indicates a complex regulatory mechanism, possibly involving metabolic pathways or enzyme-specific interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of CD37 as a central mediator in the interaction between Parameritannin A-1 and DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a potential role in cellular processes governed by DNA replication and repair.",
